{
  "data": {
    "summary": "The `models` directory is the core backend module of a Rust service that manages LLM model configuration and observability: it serves canonical model config CRUD, imports/renderers for agent CLIs (pi, opencode, claude, codex), model discovery against provider endpoints, an upstream model metadata catalog proxy, and per-model token usage statistics. `mod.rs` is the module root that wires up all `/api/models/*` axum routes and agent render/apply logic, while `discover.rs`, `catalog.rs`, and `usage.rs` are the specialized feature modules (URL/response discovery, models.dev catalog with 1h cache, and multi-source session-log aggregation). Together they form the data/API layer for provider and model management, making this one of the highest-value directories in the project.",
    "importance_score": 0.9,
    "key_files": [
      "mod.rs",
      "usage.rs",
      "discover.rs",
      "catalog.rs"
    ],
