        "name": "mod.rs",
        "summary": "Module root and routing layer for all `/api/models/*` endpoints: canonical config GET/PUT, pi import, agent renderers, apply/sync, and agent status reporting.",
        "code_purpose": "controller",
        "source_summary": "Declares handlers such as get_config, get_managed, get_agents, plus helpers pi_models_path, opencode_jsonc_path, render_agent, incremental_agent, agent_status, read_live, read_pi_defaults, read_pi_providers_summary, opencode_live_providers, read_file_optional, and test helpers temp_home/seed_pi. Uses AppState, CanonicalConfig, Agent, AgentAssignment, ApplyResult, and command_exists to translate canonical models into each agent's on-disk configuration.",
        "detailed_description": "This is the central hub of the models module, defining the axum handlers and route surface for canonical model configuration, agent (pi/opencode/claude/codex) rendering and incremental application, and live agent state inspection. It resolves per-agent config paths, reads live agent files, and merges canonical config into each agent's native format via ApplyResult. It also carries an extensive unit-test suite for live-read edge cases (temp homes, seeded pi config, missing model keys).",
        "responsibilities": [
          "Expose canonical model config routes (GET/PUT /api/models/config, import/pi)",
          "Render canonical config into pi/opencode/other agent file formats",
          "Perform incremental agent sync/apply with AgentAssignment",
          "Report per-agent status, live config, and binary availability",
          "Path resolution and safe optional file reads for agent state"
