      {
        "name": "usage.rs",
        "summary": "Aggregates per-model token usage and cost from local agent session logs (pi jsonl, opencode sqlite, claude, codex) behind `GET /api/models/usage`.",
        "code_purpose": "service",
        "source_summary": "Defines UsageQuery/UsageRow/UsageResponse/DayUsage/UsageScan and a CacheEntry-based memo cache, plus date utilities (day_label, format_iso_utc, days_to_ymd, is_leap, window_cutoff) and scanners scan_pi, scan_opencode, scan_claude, scan_codex, with find_provider_for_model and price_per_m for cost attribution. merge_row aggregates buckets keyed by model/provider.",
        "detailed_description": "The largest and most complex file in the module (~2143 lines, 74 functions, complexity 142). It scans each installed agent's local session storage, parses protocol-specific record shapes (verified field names as ground truth), buckets usage by model/day, resolves the owning provider from canonical config, and computes cost. A process-global Mutex-guarded cache with window cutoffs avoids re-scanning on every request.",
        "responsibilities": [
          "Scan pi/opencode/claude/codex session logs for token usage records",
          "Aggregate per-model token counts and costs into time-windowed buckets",
          "Compute window cutoffs and UTC date labels without external date crates",
          "Resolve model->provider mapping from canonical config",
          "Cache scan results to avoid repeated expensive disk scans"
