        "name": "catalog.rs",
        "summary": "Proxies and normalizes the upstream models.dev catalog into a CatalogResponse with a 1-hour process-global cache and in-flight request dedup.",
        "code_purpose": "specificfeature",
        "source_summary": "Defines CatalogModel/CatalogProvider/CatalogResponse/CatalogCache and normalize_catalog/normalize_model/truncate helpers, guarded by a OnceLock<tokio::sync::Mutex<Option<CatalogCache>>> with TTL Duration. Tests cover provider/model field mapping, missing-field non-panics, non-object payloads, and cache-hit-within-TTL behavior.",
        "detailed_description": "Fetches https://models.dev/api.json, normalizes loose upstream JSON into strongly-typed CatalogModel/CatalogProvider structures (with defensive handling of missing/non-object fields), and passes cost fields through unchanged. The fetch happens while holding the cache mutex so concurrent callers queue behind the in-flight fetch rather than issuing duplicate requests.",
